pt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The PC Software Industry", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about the software industry.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify information about the history of software and its characteristics in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in simple written and spoken texts about topics related to software programming and its history.  Recognizes basic ideas on programming concepts and programming history in both written and spoken passages.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Present Tense in Statements and Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use the <span class= \"strong\"> simple present tense </span>  to talk about actions that are generally true or that occur frequently.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Is the PC software industry successful thanks to the word processors?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Why are they so important?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Does the word processor have the same popularity?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They are responsible for triggering the growth of the mainframe and minicomputer software industry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In 1979, Bricklin releases the first spreadsheet program.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We use the <span class= \"strong\"> simple present tense </span>   frequently in English. Let's review first, a little bit about the verb \u2018to be' in simple present. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Affirmative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Interrogative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Interrogative with \u2018wh' questions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I am an engineer.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Am I an engineer?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Why am I an engineer?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(they, you we) You are a software developer.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Are you  a software developer?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Why are you a software developer?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(He, she, It) The processor  is new. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Is the processor new?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Why is the processor new?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<div align=\"justify\">For the other verbs different from the verb \u2018to be', we are going to follow the same grammatical structure. <br />  For regular verbs, we are just going to add an \u2018s' at the end of the verb for the third person singular (he, she, it). <br /> <br />  Example: <br /> <span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">designs</span> a spreadsheet. </span> <br /> <br />   When we want to ask a question in <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span> with a verb different from the verb \u2018to be', we use the auxiliary verb <span class=\"strong\">do</span> or <span class=\"strong\">does</span>. <br /> <br />  Example: <br /> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Do</span> you<span class=\"strong\"> like</span> developing a new software? </span> <br /> <br />   We use \u2018does' when the subject of the sentences is singular, and \u2018do' when the subject is plural. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Differences Between Spreadsheets and Word Processors", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Spreadsheets</span> and <span class=\"strong\">word processors</span> are very useful applications that allow you to carry out different tasks. Let's see how these two are different. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">SPREADSHEETS </div></span>  <div align=\"justify\"><br /> <br />We use spreadsheets to enter numeric data in order to make different calculations by using formulas. Once we process the data, we are able to see the information in an organized way. We use spreadsheets mainly for processing numeric data. <br /> <br />  <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">WORD PROCESSOR </div></span>  <br /> <br />We use word processors for writing documents that can be easily edited. We can use this application for modifying the font, the style, for adding charts or graphics, among others. We use word processors mainly for working with alphabetic data.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are two key applications that revolutionized the software industry: spreadsheet programs and word processors.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "research ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to search for information in a systematic way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Were you able to research about the PC Software Industry?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "revolutionize ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to bring radical changes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are two key applications that revolutionized the software industry: spreadsheet programs and word processors. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "trigger ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to help start something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are responsible for triggering the growth of the mainframe and minicomputer software industry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "blackboard ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a rigid surface that is used for writing with chalk or markers", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In 1979, Bricklin releases the first spreadsheet program after listening to his teacher saying that large companies divided blackboards into rows and columns for production planning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "floppy disk ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small disk that is inserted in the computer for transferring data", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: New technology advances allows users to edit on-screen and store the information on floppy disks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "edit on-screen ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to modify information by looking at the changes on a screen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: New technology advances allows users to edit on-screen and store the information on floppy disks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Make a brochure about the origins of the PC software industry.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Show specific examples of the first important applications created.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give examples of the first spreadsheet and word processing programs. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I share information about the starting point of the PC software industry.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give specific information about the origins of spreadsheet applications.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about the origins of word processing programs for microcomputers.", "type": "text"}]}]}